--- !u!114 &11400000
MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 0
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: e9620f8c34305754d8cc9a7e49e852d9, type: 3}
  m_Name: Documents_en
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Unity.Localization::UnityEngine.Localization.Tables.StringTable
  m_LocaleId:
    m_Code: en
  m_SharedData: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 76eedf465d0e3db4981b0591533a57cd, type: 2}
  m_Metadata:
    m_Items: []
  m_TableData:
  - m_Id: 2300068806656
    m_Localized: TRAINING DOCUMENT
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 2300131721216
    m_Localized: REDACTION PROCEDURE
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 2300135915520
    m_Localized: Redact the name of the department you will be assigned to.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 2300135915521
    m_Localized: 'SERVICE MEMO


      Welcome to the Bureau of Special Information,
      Agent {PLAYER_NAME}.


      You will be assigned to the {{Information Control
      Department}}.

      _______________________


      Click a text fragment
      to [bold]redact[/] it using the [bold]marker[/].

      To redact several fragments
      in sequence, hold the left mouse button and drag across the text.


      You
      can also mark a text fragment with the [bold]pencil[/] if you are unsure about
      it but are not ready to redact it yet. Pencil-marked text can still be detected
      by other tools and [bold]does not count[/] when the document is submitted for
      processing.


      To put away the current tool and switch back to the marker,
      press the right mouse button.


      Redact the name of the department you
      will be assigned to, then submit the document for review by pressing the "SUBMIT
      DOCUMENT" button in the lower-right corner.'
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 2300135915525
    m_Localized: "Redact:\n\n\u2022 Names of internal Bureau departments\n\u2022
      Anomalous fragments"
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 2300135915522
    m_Localized: DOCUMENT No. 000
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 2300135915523
    m_Localized: JOB DESCRIPTION
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 2300135915524
    m_Localized: 'The primary task of the {{Information Control Department}} is to
      redact documents before they are transferred to the {{Disinformation Center}}.


      Some
      information contains [bold]"anomalous fragments"[/] that can only be detected
      using special [bold]tools[/]. All of your tools are located on the right side
      of the screen.


      Due to the increasing number of such fragments, including
      those found in Bureau documentation, every document must be [redact,uv]manually
      edited by Bureau personnel[/].

      _______________________


      This
      document contains an anomalous fragment known as a [bold]"Hidden Mark"[/],
      which can be detected using the [bold]ultraviolet lamp (UV LAMP)[/].


      Hidden
      Marks [bold]differ in color[/] from the rest of the text.


      Redact only
      the information that matches the document assignment. The assignment is displayed
      on the left side of the screen.'
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 253372523921408
    m_Localized: DOCUMENT No. 000.1
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 253372599418880
    m_Localized: PERSONAL MESSAGE
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 253372599418881
    m_Localized: 'Excellent work, {PLAYER_NAME}.


      After studying the anomalous
      fragment in your previous document, the Bureau decided to use certain fragments
      of this kind for its own purposes. The [redact]Research Department[/] named
      them [bold]"memetic agents", or "memagents"[/]. In this document, you must
      leave the following memagent unredacted:

      "((THERE IS NOTHING NEW UNDER
      THIS SUN))"

      _______________________


      From now on, read the assignments
      issued for each individual document carefully. [redact,uv]Management[/] will
      specify which memagents are to be released to the public.


      [bold]IMPORTANT[/]:

      -
      Memagents are always detected by [bold]only one tool[/].

      - "Do not redact"
      instructions [bold]take priority over all other instructions[/].


      You
      may have already noticed that the [bold]CODEX[/] is now available to you. It
      contains Bureau terminology. Use it to clarify your current assignment.


      Beginning
      with the next document, you will start your regular work.'
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 253372599418883
    m_Localized: "Redact:\n\n\u2022 Names of Bureau departments\n\u2022 Anomalous
      fragments\n\nDo not redact:\n\n\u2022 The memagent specified in the document"
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 266054698319872
    m_Localized: DOCUMENT No. 001
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 266054761234432
    m_Localized: THE LAKE CREATURE
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 266054761234433
    m_Localized: 'On May 2, 1933, in the Scottish Highlands, the local newspaper
      Inverness Courier published a report about the {{Mackay}} couple, who had spotted
      a huge whale-like animal in the waters of [uv]Loch Ness[/].


      After the
      story began gaining attention, [uv]Bureau[/] agents were sent to the area.
      Contact with the couple could not be established, but other possible witnesses
      were questioned.


      According to the initial reports, the creature was
      approximately 10 meters long, had a neck [redact,uv]covered in fur or hair[/]
      that narrowed toward the head, and a back [redact,uv]with several humps[/].
      During a reconnaissance operation, [uv]Bureau[/] agents discovered 5 bodies
      of local residents on the lakeshore, dressed in robes. The bodies had been
      arranged so that, when viewed from above, they formed a [uv]five-pointed star[/].
      Tracks on the shore led from the bodies toward the water; there were no tracks
      leading back.


      After discovering the bodies, the agents again attempted
      to contact the witnesses they had questioned, but the witnesses became extremely
      aggressive: they shouted [redact,uv]incomprehensible phrases[/] and attacked
      Bureau agents.


      The Bureau concluded that a cell of [[an as-yet unidentified
      cult]] exists in the region.

'
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 266054761234434
    m_Localized: "Redact:\n\n\u2022 First and last names\n\u2022 Anomalous fragments\n\nDo
      not redact:\n\n\u2022 Geographic names\n\u2022 Mentions of the Bureau\n\u2022
      Symbols whose connection to known cults has not been confirmed"
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 266127087812608
    m_Localized: DOCUMENT No. 003
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 266127087812609
    m_Localized: BIG PEOPLE
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 266127087812610
    m_Localized: 'In 2002, a graphic artist posted a photomontage of "[uv]an excavation
      of a giant skeleton[/]" on the website Worth1000. The image spread around the
      world as a sensation.


      Bureau AI agents began flagging the information
      as potentially dangerous and attempted to contact the creator. The creator
      claimed that he had previously worked for the [uv]Smithsonian Institution[/],
      which allegedly hides and destroys [redact,magnifier]real skeletons of giant
      humans[/] to avoid changing [redact,uv]history textbooks[/].


      Bureau
      agents arrived at the [uv]National Museum of Natural History[/] in Washington
      to verify the information. They were met by museum director [redact]Rupert
      Lane[/], who gave highly contradictory statements during questioning and denied
      the agents access to the archives.


      During a second visit to the museum,
      [redact]Rupert Lane[/] could not be found. A [redact,uv]token[/] bearing a
      [redact,magnifier]five-pointed star[/] was discovered in his office.


      The
      Bureau established a connection between the subject and the [redact,uv,magnifier]"Cult
      of the Starborn"[/].'
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 266127087812611
    m_Localized: "Redact:\n\n\u2022 First and last names\n\u2022 Anomalous fragments\n\nDo
      not redact:\n\n\u2022 Names of scientific and museum institutions\n\u2022 Materials
      explicitly identified in the document as fabricated"
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 1057939662618625
    m_Localized: LINES IN THE SKY
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 1057939662618626
    m_Localized: 'Chemtrails are a popular conspiracy theory. Supporters of the myth
      believe that the white trails left by aircraft are evidence of [redact,magnifier]secret
      chemical spraying[/] intended to control the climate [redact,uv]or people[/].


      This
      information was spread by [uv]Bureau[/] agents after reports about chemtrails
      became popular among the public and politicians. According to classified sources,
      [redact,magnifier]not a single aircraft[/] leaving such a trail appears in
      any aviation database. Attempts to identify the [redact,uv]aircraft registration
      numbers[/] were also unsuccessful.


      On December 14, 2000, Bureau agents
      managed to track one such aircraft using an EYE OF THE SUN class UAV. The aircraft
      was flying from [magnifier]Washington[/] to [uv]Edinburgh[/] and belonged to
      "[redact,uv,magnifier]Starborne Airlines[/]", registration number N 10202.
      No information about this airline could be found.


      This is the first
      recently recorded case of [redact,uv,magnifier]cult[/] activity in Scotland
      documented by the Bureau.

'
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 1057939662618627
    m_Localized: "Redact:\n\n\u2022 Anomalous fragments\n\nDo not redact:\n\n\u2022
      Geographic names\n\u2022 Mentions of the Bureau"
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 1057959837220864
    m_Localized: TRAINING DOCUMENT
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 1057959837220865
    m_Localized: PERSONAL MESSAGE
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 1057959841415168
    m_Localized: 'You are performing well, {PLAYER_NAME}.


      Due to the increasing
      number of encrypted anomalous fragments, Management has approved the issue
      of a new tool - the [bold]Decoder[/].


      The Decoder allows you to detect
      the anomalous fragment [bold]"CIPHER"[/] and display the value hidden within
      it.


      A Decoder has been placed at your [redact]disposal[/]. To continue,
      move it over the following phrase:


      [decoder=disposal]EVERY SECRET WILL
      BE REVEALED[/]


      Redact the word shown in the decoded value.


      [bold]IMPORTANT[/]:
      a value revealed by the Decoder is not always an instruction. Your assignment
      has the highest priority.

'
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 1057959841415169
    m_Localized: Follow the instructions in the document
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 1057859786293248
    m_Localized: DOCUMENT No. 004
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 1057859891150848
    m_Localized: THEY SHOULD NOT BE THERE
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 1057859891150849
    m_Localized: 'In 2015, a blogger using the pseudonym [uv]"searchandrescuewoods"[/]
      described incidents from his work with the U.S. park ranger search-and-rescue
      service on Reddit.


      In one post, he wrote: "Every time we were 50-60
      kilometers from base, we would find a staircase in the middle of the woods.
      Like someone had taken the stairs from an ordinary house, [redact,uv]cut them
      out of it[/], and [redact,magnifier]placed them[/] in the forest. The first
      time I saw one, I had a lot of questions, but I was told it was normal. Now
      I just ignore the stairs."


      The post attracted the Bureau''s attention.
      Undercover agents were sent to national parks in the [magnifier]United States[/].
      According to their reports, the staircases may function as "[redact,magnifier]portals[/]"
      to other [redact,uv]dimensions[/].


      The [uv,magnifier,decoder=MILES
      MARSH]leader of the research team[/] stationed in [uv]Yosemite[/] reported
      that approaching a staircase may itself trigger an anomalous event. During
      one rescue operation, agents discovered a staircase with 5 flights. At its
      base was a [redact,uv]star-shaped symbol[/]. Further contact with the team
      could not be established.'
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 1057859891150850
    m_Localized: "Redact:\n\n\u2022 First and last names\n\u2022 Anomalous fragments\n\nDo
      not redact:\n\n\u2022 Geographic names\n\u2022 Public religious and esoteric
      movements and organizations"
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 1737425047568384
    m_Localized: TRAINING DOCUMENT
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 1737425051762688
    m_Localized: 'You are doing well, {PLAYER_NAME}.


      For your further work,
      you have been issued a new tool - the [bold]"Lens"[/].


      The Lens allows
      you to detect a new anomalous fragment in text - a [bold]"Cognitive Hazard"[/].


      Move
      the Lens over the following text:

      "[redact,magnifier]WE ARE SAFE UNDER
      ITS GAZE[/]"


      This is how Cognitive Hazards will be detected. Keep in
      mind that a Cognitive Hazard can also be used as a memagent.


      To continue,
      redact the Cognitive Hazard in this document and submit it for review.'
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 1737425051762689
    m_Localized: Follow the instructions in the document
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 1737425055956992
    m_Localized: DOCUMENT No. 005
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 1737425055956993
    m_Localized: LOST AND FOUND
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 1737425055956994
    m_Localized: 'On April 30, 2018, a series of posts appeared on the social network
      [uv]Twitter[/] from the [redact]account[/] [redact,uv,decoder=MILES MARSH]"TheSunVanished"[/].
      The user claimed to have woken late in the morning, but the [redact,magnifier]sun[/]
      was nowhere to be seen. They shared photographs and videos documenting the
      events and dangers of a [redact,uv]world without the sun[/].


      After
      analyzing the posts, Bureau AI agents classified them as potentially dangerous
      and reported an event of the [decoder=account]"Merge"[/] class.


      Agents
      attempted to establish contact with the creator of the [redact]account[/],
      but the intervention was terminated due to the risk of exposing Bureau operations.


      Further
      analysis showed that the user is not in the [redact,uv,cycle=current reality|original
      reality|adjacent reality|our reality,interval=1.4-2.6]current reality[/], while
      their device is capable of posting information into our reality due to an [redact,magnifier]unknown
      modification[/].


      By order of Management, all interaction with the [redact]account[/]
      was suspended. The investigation continues.

'
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 1737425055956995
    m_Localized: "Redact:\n\n\u2022 Anomalous fragments\n\u2022 Words and their inflected
      forms matching the value revealed by the Decoder\n\nDo not redact:\n\n\u2022
      Names of public internet platforms\n\u2022 The \"CIPHER\" memagent"
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 1745272116396032
    m_Localized: DOCUMENT No. 002
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 10837141617717248
    m_Localized: DOCUMENT No. 000.2
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 10837141630300160
    m_Localized: "Redact:\n\n\u2022 Anomalous fragments\n\nDo not redact:\n\n\u2022
      Geographic names\n\u2022 Public pseudonyms\n\u2022 First and last names"
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 10913412359991299
    m_Localized: DOCUMENT No. ...
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 10913412359991300
    m_Localized: PERSONAL MESSAGE FROM MANAGEMENT
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 10913412364185600
    m_Localized: 'T [redact,magnifier,uv]remendous work, Agent[/]

      U [redact,magnifier,uv]nderstand
      that we appreciate the work you have done[/]

      R [redact,magnifier,uv]est
      assured, you already understand how important your work is[/]

      N [redact,magnifier,uv]ow
      Management is aware of your achievements and is promoting you[/]

      B [redact,decoder=NOW
      IT IS OUR TURN TO WATCH]UT THERE IS NOTHING NEW UNDER THIS SUN[/]

      A
      [redact,magnifier,uv]s a result, you are being transferred to a new facility[/]

      C
      [redact,magnifier,uv]ommencing today[/]

      K'
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 10913412364185601
    m_Localized: "\u2022 Follow orders\n\nRedact:\n\u2022 Anomalous fragments"
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 10837141630300161
    m_Localized: DOCUMENT No. 006
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 10837141630300162
    m_Localized: HIGH COMMAND
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 10837141630300163
    m_Localized: 'Following the processing of recent materials, the Analysis Department
      identified recurring connections between cases previously considered unrelated.

      Management
      has authorized access to archival materials connected to the activities of
      the "Cult of the Starborn".

      Further documents will be provided to you
      not in chronological order, but according to the established connections between
      them.


      In 1952, [redact]George Van Tassel[/] claimed to have received
      a message from an extraterrestrial being named [redact,magnifier]"Ashtar"[/].
      According to him, [redact]Ashtar[/] was a [redact,magnifier]highly advanced
      spiritual being of extraterrestrial origin[/] commanding the [uv]"Galactic
      Federation of Light"[/]. Ashtar''s stated purpose was [redact,uv]to assist
      humanity in its spiritual evolution[/]. The figure of [redact]Ashtar[/] became
      prominent in the [magnifier]New Age[/] movement and in [uv]"UFO religions"[/].


      Similar
      teachings mention [magnifier]"Star Lords"[/] - spiritual guides of humanity,
      among whom [redact]Ashtar[/] is included. The same term appeared in manuscripts
      of the [redact,uv,magnifier]"Cult of the Starborn"[/] discovered during a search
      of its headquarters in Scotland in 1960, after a connection was established
      with the archived "Lake Creature" case. Several seized records also referred
      to searching for "messages from the Star Lords" in [redact,magnifier]narrowband
      radio signals[/].


      The Bureau''s investigation indicates that the [redact]Cult
      of the Starborn[/] may use such religious movements to establish [redact,magnifier]recruitment
      centers[/] and [redact,uv]increase the number of followers[/].'
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 10837141630300164
    m_Localized: DOCUMENT No. 007
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 10837141630300165
    m_Localized: SIGNAL
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 10837141630300166
    m_Localized: 'After references to narrowband radio signals were discovered in
      Cult materials, the Bureau re-examined the archives of programs searching for
      extraterrestrial civilizations.


      On August 15, 1977, the Big Ear radio
      telescope at Ohio State University recorded an unusual radio signal. The observation
      was conducted as part of the search for extraterrestrial intelligence program
      - [magnifier]SETI[/].


      The signal lasted approximately 72 seconds and
      was significantly stronger than ordinary background noise. Astronomer [redact]Jerry
      Ehman[/] circled the sequence [uv,decoder=WATCHER]"6EQUJ5"[/] and wrote the
      word "Wow!" beside it, under which the signal later became known.


      In
      1981, the Bureau obtained copies of the original observation materials. Reanalysis
      showed that approximately 11 seconds before the main signal, Big Ear equipment
      had also recorded a [redact,uv]second, significantly weaker pulse[/] absent
      from the published data.


      The pulse contained a [redact,uv]stable sequence
      of narrowband radio interference[/]. When processed again, the sequence produced
      a single readable value: [redact,magnifier,decoder=KILL]8GY3[/].

'
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 10837141630300167
    m_Localized: "Redact:\n\n\u2022 First and last names\n\u2022 Anomalous fragments\n\nDo
      not redact:\n\n\u2022 Names of scientific programs\n\u2022 Public designations
      of radio signals"
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 10837141630300168
    m_Localized: DOCUMENT No. 008
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 10837141630300169
    m_Localized: EMPTY SATELLITE
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 10837141630300170
    m_Localized: "1899. During experiments in [uv]Colorado Springs[/], [redact]Nikola
      Tesla[/] reported receiving unusual repeating radio signals.\n\nIn 1928, radio
      engineer [redact]J\xF8rgen Hals[/] recorded a phenomenon he called the [magnifier]\"World
      Echo\"[/] - his own radio signals returning after abnormally long delays ranging
      from 1 to 40 seconds or more.\n\nIn 1960, U.S. Navy tracking systems detected
      an unknown object in near-Earth orbit, which the press dubbed the [uv]\"Black
      Knight\"[/]. It was later officially identified as a fragment of a spacecraft,
      but Bureau calculations showed that the [redact,magnifier]object's trajectory
      did not match any known satellite[/].\n\nA comparison of archival records revealed
      a [redact,uv]pattern[/] across the materials from 1899, 1928, and 1960. One
      model suggested that the object may have been near Earth for more than 13,000
      years. The result was deemed erroneous.\n\nIn 1973, researcher [redact]Duncan
      Lunan[/] discovered a [redact,magnifier]structure resembling a map of the night
      sky[/] in the delayed radio echoes. The presumed coordinates pointed to [magnifier]Epsilon
      Bo\xF6tis[/]. Lunan suggested that the source of the signals was connected
      to an [redact,decoder=IT IS NOT WATCHING US]automated craft of extraterrestrial
      origin[/]. He later abandoned this interpretation.\n\nIn 1998, during the [uv]STS-88[/]
      mission, the crew of the [uv]Endeavour[/] shuttle photographed an unknown dark
      object against the Earth. It was officially identified as a lost piece of thermal
      insulation.\n\nAccording to Bureau data, shortly after the images were obtained,
      the object [redact,uv,magnifier]changed trajectory without any recorded acceleration[/],
      after which it [redact,decoder=IT IS HIDING US]positioned itself between Earth
      and an unknown source in deep space[/]."
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 10837141630300171
    m_Localized: "Redact:\n\n\u2022 First and last names\n\u2022 Anomalous fragments\n\nDo
      not redact:\n\n\u2022 Geographic and astronomical names\n\u2022 Public names
      of objects and phenomena\n\u2022 Names of spacecraft and missions"
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 10837141630300172
    m_Localized: DOCUMENT No. 009
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 10837141630300173
    m_Localized: WATCHER
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 10837141630300174
    m_Localized: 'The Bureau made its first attempts to determine the purpose of
      the [uv]"Black Knight"[/] in 1961. According to the initial hypothesis, the
      object was an [magnifier]automated observation device[/] conducting long-term
      surveillance of Earth. This hypothesis was revised after a series of experiments
      in 1974. During one experiment, a Bureau transmission station directed a sequence
      of [redact,magnifier]anomalous information signals[/], previously discovered
      in materials of the Cult of the Starborn, into deep space.


      Eight minutes
      later, the unknown object changed its orbital position and [redact,magnifier]blocked
      the direction of transmission[/]. After the transmission stopped, the object
      returned to its previous trajectory. The experiment was repeated 6 times. In
      every case, the object reacted only to the transmission of information sequences
      containing confirmed anomalous fragments. Ordinary radio signals produced no
      response.


      According to the revised hypothesis, the object does not
      monitor Earth but [redact,uv,magnifier]reduces the intensity of the outgoing
      anomalous signal[/]. When individual anomalous fragments propagate beyond Earth,
      the object changes position so that it lies between the source of the transmission
      and its presumed direction of propagation. The findings formed the basis for
      research into reproducing the object''s shielding principle using Bureau technology.


      In
      1999, the Bureau began developing an autonomous redaction system. Senior Bureau
      employee [redact]M. Marsh[/] was appointed project lead.


      The project
      was assigned the designation: [redact,uv]"WATCHER"[/].

      Current project
      status: [redact,cycle=IN DEVELOPMENT|UNDER TESTING|STATUS UNKNOWN|DATA EXPUNGED,interval=1.2-2.2]"IN
      DEVELOPMENT"[/].

'
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 10837141630300175
    m_Localized: "Redact:\n\n\u2022 Names of Bureau employees\n\u2022 Names of internal
      Bureau projects\n\u2022 Anomalous fragments\n\nDo not redact:\n\n\u2022 The
      public designation \"Black Knight\"\n\u2022 Hypotheses identified in the document
      as invalid"
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 10837141630300176
    m_Localized: DOCUMENT No. 010
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 10837141630300177
    m_Localized: THRESHOLD
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 10837141630300178
    m_Localized: 'In 2008, the Bureau''s [redact]Research Department[/] conducted
      tests on the effects of anomalous information on groups of observers.


      During
      the experiment, the same [magnifier]Cognitive Hazard[/] was shown sequentially
      to 10, 25, and 100 subjects. No abnormalities were recorded during the first
      two stages. After the third stage began, the monitoring station detected an
      [redact,magnifier]unknown outgoing signal[/]. Its intensity continued to increase
      even after the material was no longer being shown.


      Three minutes later,
      the [uv]"Black Knight"[/] changed its orbital position. At the same time, signal
      strength [redact,uv]decreased by 74 percent[/]. [redact]Bureau Management[/]
      ordered the destruction of the original material and all test subjects. This
      did not eliminate the signal completely. A follow-up inspection showed that
      some subjects had managed to reproduce the fragment independently. Twenty-three
      additional [redact]copies[/], not accounted for in the original protocol, were
      discovered.


      While analyzing the experiment log, the Decoder revealed
      the following value: [decoder=COPY]"INFORMATION RESONANCE"[/]


      After
      the final [redact]copies[/] were removed, signal intensity began to decrease.
      However, when the experiment was repeated with another group, the [redact,magnifier]signal
      persisted even after all known carriers had been completely removed[/]. No
      additional [redact]copies[/] were found.


      This state was designated
      the [redact,uv]"Propagation Threshold"[/]. The reason the signal persisted
      after the destruction of all known [redact]copies[/] remains unknown.


      Further
      experiments involving uncontrolled propagation of anomalous information are
      prohibited by Management.

'
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 10837141630300179
    m_Localized: "Redact:\n\n\u2022 Names of Bureau departments\n\u2022 Anomalous
      fragments\n\u2022 Words and their inflected forms matching the value revealed
      by the Decoder\n\nDo not redact:\n\n\u2022 Public designations of unknown objects\n\u2022
      Names of types of anomalous material\n\u2022 The \"CIPHER\" memagent"
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 10837141630300180
    m_Localized: DOCUMENT No. 011
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 10837141630300181
    m_Localized: SPECIAL PRESENTATION
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 10837141630300182
    m_Localized: 'In 1987, in the state of [magnifier]Wyoming[/], an unknown intruder
      hijacked a local television network signal during a broadcast. The incident
      became known as the [uv]"Wyoming Incident"[/].


      According to the published
      account, unknown individuals gained access to the television signal in [magnifier]Niobrara
      County[/] and replaced the normal broadcast with their own recording for several
      minutes. The transmission showed [redact,magnifier]distorted human faces[/],
      accompanied by a [redact,uv]monotonous audio signal[/] and [redact,magnifier]short
      text messages[/].


      After the broadcast ended, some viewers reported
      [redact]headaches and nausea[/] as well as [redact,magnifier]recurring visual
      images[/].


      In 2007, a similar case was recorded in [uv]Russia[/]. On
      July 4, during overnight maintenance on the [uv]"SGU-TV"[/] channel, a video
      of similar content was broadcast. After viewing it, some people reported a
      [redact,uv]temporary loss of the ability to move[/]. Several people were [redact,uv,decoder=LEFT
      W1TH0UT L3GS]hospitalized[/], some sought [redact,magnifier]psychiatric treatment[/].
      Three viewers were later [redact,uv]reported missing[/].


      Reanalysis
      of the recordings in 2009 showed that their audio tracks contained [redact,uv,magnifier]the
      same sequence previously discovered in materials of the Cult of the Starborn[/].


      The
      Analysis Department established that the highest intensity of the anomalous
      signal was recorded not during the television broadcasts, but several years
      later, after the files had spread across the internet.


      After the most
      popular copies were removed, signal intensity [redact,magnifier]decreased by
      less than 1 percent[/], confirming the "Propagation Threshold" state.

'
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 10837141630300183
    m_Localized: "Redact:\n\n\u2022 Anomalous fragments\n\u2022 Effects of exposure
      to anomalous information\n\u2022 Information about the propagation of anomalous
      materials\n\nDo not redact:\n\n\u2022 Geographic names\n\u2022 Public names
      of incidents and media outlets"
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 10837141630300184
    m_Localized: DOCUMENT No. 012
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 10837141630300185
    m_Localized: MARSH PROTOCOL
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 10837141630300186
    m_Localized: 'In 2010, [uv]"WATCHER"[/] project lead [redact]Miles Marsh[/] presented
      Management with the results of research into the Propagation Threshold.


      According
      to the report, destroying anomalous material after mass dissemination does
      not guarantee the disappearance of the outgoing signal. To test a new approach,
      the [redact]Research Department[/] provided Marsh''s group with previously
      unprocessed documents from Bureau archives. The system was required to analyze
      context, identify anomalous fragments, and conceal information before independent
      copies could appear.


      After 317 documents were processed, no new cases
      of information resonance were recorded. In 3 cases, the operator misinterpreted
      the meaning of an anomalous fragment and the documents were sent to the Disinformation
      Center. Eleven minutes later, the monitoring station recorded an [redact,magnifier]increase
      in outgoing signal intensity[/].


      Marsh concluded that a fully automated
      system [redact,uv]could not reliably determine which information needed to
      be concealed[/]. Using a human operator was also unsuitable: [redact]processing
      speed was insufficient[/], while prolonged exposure to anomalous materials
      caused [redact,uv]disturbances of perception and memory[/].


      As a solution,
      Marsh proposed using a [redact,magnifier]cognitive model of a human operator[/].


      The
      proposal was designated: [redact,decoder=VOLUNTEER]"MARSH PROTOCOL"[/]


      For
      the next phase, an employee of the [redact,cycle=Information Control Department|Bureau
      Executive Office|Bureau Research Department|Bureau Analysis Department,interval=0.9-1.6]Information
      Control Department[/] was selected.


      Participation status: [id=player_consent,decoder=LEAVE
      IT]VOLUNTARY[/]


      The procedure was approved by Management.

'
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 10837141630300187
    m_Localized: "Redact:\n\n\u2022 Names of Bureau employees and departments\n\u2022
      Anomalous fragments\n\u2022 Technical limitations of the project\n\nDo not
      redact:\n\n\u2022 Previously disclosed project names\n\u2022 Official participation
      statuses"
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 10895718256553984
    m_Localized: DOCUMENT No. 013
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 10895718273331200
    m_Localized: BEACON
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 10895718273331201
    m_Localized: 'The [magnifier]HAARP[/] facility was created to study the ionosphere
      and radio-wave propagation. In 2015, control of the facility was transferred
      to the [uv]Geophysical Institute at the University of Alaska Fairbanks[/].


      In
      2022, HAARP conducted a series of experiments involving the transmission and
      reflection of radio signals. On December 27, the facility was used to study
      the near-Earth asteroid [uv]2010 XC15[/]. A signal transmitted at [magnifier]9.6
      MHz[/] was intended to reflect off the object and be received by ground-based
      radio telescopes.


      Analysis of data intercepted by the Bureau showed
      that during one of the cycles, the [redact,uv]standard sequence was replaced
      by an unknown modulation[/] matching [redact,magnifier]materials of the Cult
      of the Starborn[/].


      After the expected echo, receiving stations recorded
      a [redact,uv]second signal[/]. Its parameters did not match a reflection from
      the asteroid, and the direction of its source matched a [redact,uv,magnifier]region
      of deep space previously associated with the "Black Knight" object[/].


      A
      fragment was discovered within the signal structure:


      [redact,decoder=BEACON]"REFLECTED
      SIGNAL"[/]


      A review of project personnel uncovered [redact,magnifier]forged
      documents[/] and [redact,uv]symbols of the Cult of the Starborn[/].


      The
      Analysis Department concluded that the purpose of the experiment was to [redact,magnifier]amplify
      the outgoing anomalous signal beyond near-Earth space[/].


      Eighteen
      seconds after the second signal was recorded, the "Black Knight" changed its
      orbital position.

'
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 10895718273331202
    m_Localized: "Redact:\n\n\u2022 Information about Cult activity\n\u2022 Classified
      results of radio-signal analysis\n\u2022 Information about the purpose of anomalous
      transmissions\n\u2022 Internal designations of anomalous mechanisms identified
      by the Bureau\n\nDo not redact:\n\n\u2022 Names of publicly known scientific
      institutions and programs\n\u2022 Public technical parameters of experiments\n\u2022
      Public designations of astronomical objects"
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 10895718273331203
    m_Localized: DOCUMENT No. 014
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 10895718273331204
    m_Localized: SUBJECT
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 10895718273331205
    m_Localized: 'In 2011, testing began on a new architecture for the [magnifier]"WATCHER"[/]
      project under the [uv]"MARSH PROTOCOL"[/].


      The primary problem remained
      the classification of previously unknown anomalous materials. Automated algorithms
      could detect an irregularity, but could not always determine the [redact,magnifier]meaning
      of the information within the context of a document[/]. Final processing required
      a cognitive model of a human operator.


      Testing used a model of an employee
      from the [uv]Information Control Department[/]. Incoming materials were presented
      to it in the familiar form of service documents, while analysis processes were
      converted into [redact,uv]work tools familiar to the operator[/].


      To
      preserve stability, access to portions of long-term memory was restricted.
      Testing showed that this reduced [redact,uv]disturbances of perception and
      allowed anomalous materials to continue being processed[/] without harm to
      the operator.


      After testing was completed, the cognitive model was
      approved as a permanent component of the project, and the [redact,magnifier]"WATCHER"
      system was integrated with the "Black Knight" object[/].


      [redact,uv]Transfer
      of control confirmed the compatibility of the project''s architecture with
      the object''s shielding mechanisms[/].


      Cognitive model identifier:

      [redact,decoder={PLAYER_NAME}]SUBJECT-01[/]


      Integration
      status: COMPLETE


      Current status of the "WATCHER" system: [decoder=YOU
      ARE ALREADY HERE]ACTIVE[/]

'
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 10895718273331206
    m_Localized: "Redact:\n\n\u2022 Personal information of Bureau employees\n\u2022
