  - m_Id: 10895718273331207
    m_Localized: DOCUMENT No. 015
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 10895718273331208
    m_Localized: DEAD INTERNET
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 10895718273331209
    m_Localized: 'The [magnifier]"Dead Internet Theory"[/] proposes that a significant
      portion of online information is created by automated systems without direct
      human involvement. The spread of [uv]generative models[/] has led to a sharp
      increase in the amount of automatically generated text and imagery.


      Current
      Bureau monitoring has identified [redact,uv]anomalous fragments in materials
      created by several independent models[/]. None of the detected fragments had
      ever been recorded before.


      Analysis showed that the systems [redact,magnifier]do
      not copy known anomalous materials, but reproduce the principle by which they
      are formed[/].


      A review of training sources revealed [redact,uv]materials
      of the Cult of the Starborn in several publicly available datasets[/]. Their
      dissemination began long before generative systems came into widespread use.


      After
      being trained on contaminated data, the models began independently generating
      [redact,magnifier]new variants of anomalous fragments[/]. The rate at which
      they appear continues to increase.


      The [magnifier]"WATCHER"[/] system
      has been placed in continuous shielding mode. Despite the redistribution of
      resources within the "Black Knight" object, the monitoring station recorded
      a [redact,uv]sustained increase in the outgoing signal[/].


      A sequence
      was detected in the response signal:


      [redact,decoder=YOU ARE THE DOOR]SYNCHRONIZATION[/]


      In
      every confirmed case, immediately before a new anomalous fragment was generated,
      the system displayed the same line:


      [id=beacon_spreader,redact,uv,decoder=L3AVE]SHARE[/]'
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 10895718273331210
    m_Localized: "Redact:\n\n\u2022 Anomalous fragments\n\u2022 Information about
